troyed by you.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.869,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-67-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4066027","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6ba546a5c7cc7c1335cbacb2d1492b9a89001b104068c093d0807b63d02414ae","compact":"dea56d7ca37a04071f69cd03ceed753e240d75dccdb6f8e24ffe43eee65803f6","nasal":"dea56d7ca37a04071f69cd03ceed753e240d75dccdb6f8e24ffe43eee65803f6"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-66-28","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":66,"verse":28,"english":"These foremost of monkeys assembled, who wish for your welfare, shall, with intent mind, perform acts tending to your weal,-so that you mayst succeed in your undertaking.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.794,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-67-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4066028","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"18643d54d90513787368cee5a2817fcf1a49c9ff92291cff82c70d73ec9cc4e8","compact":"f4765fca1b6edc64e446da900408d19d895f7f838bf6d4079a8ae1190279f635","nasal":"66a04be5e6666cd2daf7a9916648600be13995cd770cab614f38ce8deb7c89d8"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-66-29","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":66,"verse":29,"english":"By the grace of the saints, and with the permission of the aged monkeys, and by the blessing of the superiors, do you bound over the mighty main.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.772,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-67-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4066029","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"88b61ff80ec4320503e3a16de19eb909021b36574790ef9fb09a8ffffcfdc4c4","compact":"a800c4efb97a0630c6d0948e2572e700047306a9b9b879a601b283302912b33e","nasal":"a800c4efb97a0630c6d0948e2572e700047306a9b9b879a601b283302912b33e"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-66-30","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":66,"verse":30,"english":"Till you return, we shall stay on one leg. The lives of all these rangers of the forest shall go along with you. *i.e. practise austerities on your behalf.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.845,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-67-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4066030","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6dae598e30122fb0c2510aefba82cf51d340a92086b6fa1d57ebaf2409c56e99","compact":"09f167d46f110e41f4290c04a5edfc0e1b5f414447e80894f4be3e756eb24996","nasal":"09f167d46f110e41f4290c04a5edfc0e1b5f414447e80894f4be3e756eb24996"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-66-31","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":66,"verse":31,"english":"Then that tiger-like monkey said to those rangers of the woods, None in this world would be able to sustain my impetus in the act of bounding.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.585,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-67-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4066031","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ac37ec26d5c002f554a56af52ffb68965922aff1a66041eb6d39b0fd0668b49b","compact":"5f0a2bc215afe5e5d8c60056d82525053c58636eeb39ea851a9eb540e14ef8f9","nasal":"5f0a2bc215afe5e5d8c60056d82525053c58636eeb39ea851a9eb540e14ef8f9"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-66-32","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":66,"verse":32,"english":"Here are these summits, firm and spacious, of this mountain, Mahendra, thronged with crags. I shall rush forward from these summits of Mahendra, interspersed with trees and adorned with masses of ore.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.914,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-67-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4066032","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a4e4be683d7ac654f8bd6c35fbf9716258758f887836f73827bc1b5c1c37a23d","compact":"8a5da8fd8e3e620e99d1c726af66dddaa5d5c9ac201e4cc99c4ec84a734f9f67","nasal":"2473f0ae37975382d45f3bec892b90a6cda11c00e0008e91f287ad9752d18dad"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-66-33","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":66,"verse":33,"english":"As I leap over a hundred Yojanas, these mighty summits shall sustain my impetus.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.464,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-67-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4066033","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8aac92aec7a44133f9051991f2974d4333f109d6085c37819aeb1dc220e82697","compact":"50eda78a0bab1c64278ef8aa47205d5461c0b5b6a3a023b16aaf70772589a609","nasal":"fc7baad0057454c71e7837348fbcfe85e0ffb91dc396d6ad657d69dc0d1dac13"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-66-34","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":66,"verse":34,"english":"Then he equalling the Wind, that monkey, the son of the Wind-god, pounder of enemies, ascended that best of mountains, Mahendra; covered with with various trees and flowers, furnished with swards; ranged by deer; containing plants and blossoms with trees bearing fruits and flowers daily; having tigers and lions and infuriated elephants; swarming with maddened birds; and abounding with fountains. Ascending (Mahendra), that foremost of monkeys endued with exceeding strength, and resembling Mahendra himself in prowess, began to range from one mighty summit to another.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-67-31"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4066034","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a83322de46d8102f0a7d0b3bcbc5cb8987672044c9db680fa91b81e70e4ca037","compact":"43f9e437063732c2a9f9c0da28e86f50c6d903619cf316b37e31b09f8f1738b2","nasal":"c5cf9c7ebcef47a0baf9030720025abdf7b2948b4fc663d3632c06011a856322"}},