6-43","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":66,"verse":43,"english":"With its serpents hissing, with their bodies half issuing (from their holes), the mountain seemed as if it shone with pennons displayed. And the heap of crags forsaken by saints exercised with fear and agitation, looked doleful, like a wayfarer left in a vast forest by his companions.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.87,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-67-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4066043","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b73f74c1322801355e880163135337055221fd0e772893620155ddce08df5e97","compact":"eed45083753f75a533c6af148fa760af8c2f0c648072ae49f0ec6dd581e7a312","nasal":"40f60c54db56bfbdf29a65a344952f8305176d422e5e7bd512232273032d1b21"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-66-44","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":66,"verse":44,"english":"That intelligent, magnanimous and heroic monkey-destroyer of hostile heroes, endowed with speed, concentrating his soul on his energy, mentally went to Lankā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.904,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-67-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4066044","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f87f5dcf976e1350dbda110372daeac6bd166be5b1d7042985512cc78fb441f4","compact":"c82bcb47034fb2257f9cf2d823d6cf1287a34ade9c2373c74c21dc7c290791d2","nasal":"300a78cc9f193d1caa3b80682b9aa655f20dcba16a66fa3916b85059027e3302"}}]
